avcodec/liboapvenc: create the metadata handler with a description

oapvm_create() took a description argument in OpenAPV 1.0, and this still
calls the older form, so FFmpeg does not build against any current
OpenAPV: "too few arguments to function call, expected 2, have 1".

Pass a zeroed description, whose NULL allocator interface means the
standard C one; oapvm_create() rejects a NULL description outright, so
the argument cannot simply be NULL. Guarded on OAPV_VER_APISET so the
older libraries still build.

Made against n9.0.1; master has the same code.
---
--- a/libavcodec/liboapvenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/liboapvenc.c
@@ -509,7 +509,16 @@
     }
 
     /* create metadata handler */
+#if OAPV_VER_APISET >= 1
+    {
+        /* Zeroed: a NULL allocator interface means the standard C one.
+           oapvm_create() rejects a NULL description outright. */
+        oapvm_cdesc_t mcdsc = { 0 };
+        apv->mid = oapvm_create(&mcdsc, &ret);
+    }
+#else
     apv->mid = oapvm_create(&ret);
+#endif
     if (apv->mid == NULL || OAPV_FAILED(ret)) {
         av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "cannot create OAPV metadata handler\n");
         return AVERROR_EXTERNAL;
